### Summary

The goal model is structured to handle both food delivery and dish retrieval, considering various scenarios and cooperation possibilities. Each goal is decomposed into sub-goals and tasks that reflect the mission's requirements, ensuring flexibility and robustness in execution. The use of AND and OR decompositions, along with parallel and sequential execution annotations, captures the complexity of the mission effectively.
